tags: ["AI", "Agent", "Progressive Disclosure"]
badge: "Agents"
---

The agent's knowledge files are a small table of contents. Instead of using context .md files with decoupling, we can split the .md. With this, you will have a small table of contents with links and detailed context. This raises the overall content. So the knowledge is short and focused content, and the per-usage context will be decreased and accuracy will be increased.
The disadvantage here is that the complexity increases, which can cause issues: the agent may not be able to use a context, or may choose the wrong one, and maintenance also increases.
